{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"As of November 6, 2026:\n\n- **Application:** File an exemptive application through EDGAR identifying relief beyond Rule 6c-11 and supporting statutory findings. Staff reviews it and may request amendments.\n- **Notice:** If review is satisfactory, the SEC publishes notice describing the requested relief and allowing at least 25 days for hearing requests.\n- **Order:** After notice, the SEC may grant relief if applicable standards are met and no hearing is ordered. A hearing request does not itself require a hearing.\n\n**Rule 0-5 expedited review** is available upon request for applications substantially identical to **two applications granted within the preceding three years**, with required comparisons and certifications.\n\n**Worth knowing:** Its **45-day clock concerns issuance of notice—not a final exemptive order**. It pauses for staff modification requests; eligibility concerns can remove an application from expedited review. It therefore does not establish a universal total approval time. [Rule 0-5](https://www.law.cornell.edu/cfr/text/17/270.0-5)"}}
